# Bearer tokens for lucent (/memory/*, /graph/*) and comms (the gateway).
# Empty = bypass mode (a startup warning is logged and all routes accept
# any/no Authorization header). Set both in production. 43+ chars
# recommended. COMMS_BEARER_TOKEN must equal the same var in the repo
# root's .env — bots authenticate to comms with that value.
# The memory store keeps no copy of this and compares nothing against it.
# Each holder — every mind, every service, the nightly pruner — presents its
# own value here, and the store checks it against its credentials table. Mint
# one per holder with `PUT /credentials/{holder}` using the admin token below,
# then put that holder's value in its own environment. A holder with no
# credential is refused; there is no shared value and no bypass.
LUCENT_BEARER_TOKEN=
# Same rule at the gateway: comms keeps no copy and this is each holder's own
# value, minted with `PUT /credentials/{holder}`. The one shared value that
# every mind, every surface bot and the boys' boxes all presented is no longer
# accepted at all, and leaving this unset no longer opens the gateway — it
# refuses.
COMMS_BEARER_TOKEN=

# Admin-only bearer for schema-mutation / registry-admin endpoints on each
# service. Only hive-tools (or another trusted maintainer caller) should
# hold these. Leave empty to disable those endpoints entirely.
LUCENT_ADMIN_BEARER_TOKEN=
# The one credential that can change a Mind's soul, on /graph/soul. Neither
# the service bearer nor the admin bearer is accepted there: hive-tools holds
# admin, and hive-tools is the path a sub-mind's verdict travels. Unset locks
# the route (503) rather than opening it.
LUCENT_SOUL_BEARER_TOKEN=
COMMS_ADMIN_BEARER_TOKEN=
# The one credential that may change a conversation's name, presented in the
# X-Rename-Token header on top of the service bearer. Held apart from
# COMMS_BEARER_TOKEN on purpose: that one is on every surface bot and every mind
# container including the kids' machines, and a copy of this one escaping into a
# log or a screenshot is worth exactly one renamed conversation. Every client
# that renames — the browser terminal, the Telegram bot, the health app — already
# holds this value as TERMINAL_LABELS_TOKEN, so set it to the same string.
# Unset REFUSES every rename rather than falling open.
COMMS_RENAME_TOKEN=

# Optional — only if you're using the SMS inbound webhook (see
# nervous-system/docs/sms-inbound.md). Signs incoming webhook requests.
# SMS_INBOUND_HMAC_SECRET=
